#: ../../source/docs/selecting-a-frame.rst:5 b4175490914c44cabaaf92bfe0ee52b3
msgid "Selecting a Rover Frame"
msgstr "选择 Rover 车架"

#: ../../source/docs/selecting-a-frame.rst:7 35d24ee374b74e1f8ed57d821f45bc62
msgid ""
"Building a Rover-based vehicle project from the ground up is entirely "
"feasible, but it's recommended to start with an existing RC vehicle. "
"Utilizing this approach provides an immediate head start, furnishing you "
"with a pre-assembled frame, complete with wired motor and ESC, thereby "
"streamlining your construction process."
msgstr ""
"从零开始构建基于 Rover 的车辆项目是完全可行的，但建议从现有的 RC "
"车辆开始。采用这种方法可以立即获得先机，为您提供预组装好的车架、已配线的电机和 ESC，从而简化构建过程。"

#: ../../source/docs/selecting-a-frame.rst:10 5ad3903a52ef41498f2d0682c949cebd
msgid ""
"If you choose to begin with a pre-assembled RC vehicle, the main areas of "
"focus should be the successful integration of key components. These "
"components typically include the autopilot system, GPS module, telemetry "
"radio, and an RC Transmitter. The integration process involves carefully "
"mounting these components on the RC vehicle, ensuring reliable connections, "
"and configuring settings as required."
msgstr ""
"如果您选择从预组装的 RC 车辆开始，主要关注点应是关键组件的成功集成。这些组件通常包括自动驾驶仪系统、GPS 模块、数传电台和 RC "
"发射机。集成过程包括仔细地将这些组件安装到 RC 车辆上，确保连接可靠，并根据需要进行设置配置。"

#: ../../source/docs/selecting-a-frame.rst:14 82cd6c6dd26543b487ad653f1b62baaf
msgid ""
"Keep in mind that the list of required hardware can vary depending on the "
"complexity and specific requirements of your project. For instance, you "
"might need to incorporate additional sensors for obstacle avoidance, "
"environmental monitoring, or a companion computer for advanced processing "
"tasks."
msgstr ""
"请记住，所需硬件列表可能因项目的复杂性和具体要求而有所不同。例如，您可能需要集成用于避障、环境监测的额外传感器，或用于高级处理任务的伴飞计算机。"

#: ../../source/docs/selecting-a-frame.rst:17 7c819797c5234047aabe347b1dca8297
msgid ""
"Moreover, it's important to consider the spatial constraints of your RC "
"vehicle while deciding on these components. Smaller RC vehicles may require "
"more compact hardware or innovative mounting solutions. On the other hand, "
"larger vehicles might offer more freedom in terms of component selection and"
" placement, but could present their own unique challenges."
msgstr ""
"此外，在决定这些组件时，务必考虑 RC 车辆的空间限制。较小的 RC "
"车辆可能需要更紧凑的硬件或创新的安装方案。另一方面，较大的车辆在组件选择和放置方面可能提供更多自由度，但也可能带来其独特的挑战。"

#: ../../source/docs/selecting-a-frame.rst:26 5db7e90ec3014ff7b2cc9a5296c2b5c4
msgid "Choosing the Right Scale"
msgstr "选择合适的比例尺寸"

#: ../../source/docs/selecting-a-frame.rst:28 322adcc86d0448dbbc7bae9ebdb4808e
msgid ""
"For those leaning towards a classic car design, a 1/10 scale RC car is a "
"superb choice. 1/10 scale vehicles are often recommended due to their "
"sizable dimensions that facilitate easier maintenance and hassle-free "
"installation of supplementary equipment, such as companion computers."
msgstr ""
"对于倾向经典汽车设计的用户，1/10 比例 RC 车是绝佳选择。1/10 比例车辆因其较大的尺寸而被普遍推荐，便于维护和安装伴飞计算机等辅助设备。"

#: ../../source/docs/selecting-a-frame.rst:31 9a7600ee9d8648acac5840505913f3e8
msgid ""
"Although the compactness of smaller-scale vehicles (1/16 or `1/18 scale "
"<https://hobbyking.com/en_us/1-18-brushless-4wd-stadium-truck-w-18amp-"
"system.html>`__) might impose a more challenging setup process, the image "
"gallery on this wiki reassures you that overcoming this challenge is wholly "
"attainable with some effort."
msgstr ""
"尽管较小比例车辆（1/16 或 `1/18 比例 <https://hobbyking.com/en_us/1-18-brushless-4wd-"
"stadium-truck-w-18amp-system.html>`__）的紧凑性可能带来更具挑战性的安装过程，但本 Wiki "
"的图库向您保证，只需付出一些努力，这一挑战完全可以克服。"

#: ../../source/docs/selecting-a-frame.rst:33 821db3d04f7043a1b28112ea0cd8a3c3
msgid ""
"For those who favor slow, skid-steering rovers, the `Wild Thumper "
"<https://www.robotgear.com.au/Product.aspx/Discontinued/1978-Wild-"
"Thumper-6WD-Chassis-Black-34-1-gear-ratio>`__ models come highly recommended"
" by the community."
msgstr ""
"对于偏好低速差速转向 Rover 的用户，社区强烈推荐 `Wild Thumper "
"<https://www.robotgear.com.au/Product.aspx/Discontinued/1978-Wild-"
"Thumper-6WD-Chassis-Black-34-1-gear-ratio>`__ 系列车型。"

#: ../../source/docs/selecting-a-frame.rst:36 40dbb45621cd404ead8accb343cfedb8
msgid "Comparing 2WD and 4WD"
msgstr "两驱与四驱的比较"

#: ../../source/docs/selecting-a-frame.rst:38 809e1ce8414b4d7f90edf10b91fafb29
msgid ""
"Performance-wise, `2WD <https://hobbyking.com/en_us/basher-bsr-"
"bz-222-1-10-2wd-racing-buggy-arr.html>`__ vehicles tend to outperform their "
"`4WD <https://hobbyking.com/en_us/turnigy-trooper-sct-4x4-1-10-brushless-"
"short-course-truck-arr.html>`__ counterparts. This is because their simpler "
"mechanical design results in prolonged battery life compared to an "
"equivalent 2WD model. However, for high-speed cornering or navigation on "
"uneven terrains, 4WD reigns supreme."
msgstr ""
"在性能方面，`两驱 <https://hobbyking.com/en_us/basher-bsr-bz-222-1-10-2wd-racing-"
"buggy-arr.html>`__ 车辆往往优于其 `四驱 <https://hobbyking.com/en_us/turnigy-trooper-"
"sct-4x4-1-10-brushless-short-course-truck-arr.html>`__ "
"对应款，因为其更简单的机械设计相比同等两驱车型能延长电池续航。但在高速过弯或不平整地形导航时，四驱则占据主导优势。"

#: ../../source/docs/selecting-a-frame.rst:42 ff769c32e03f4ca7b3f428a67079c983
msgid "Additional Recommendations"
msgstr "额外建议"

#: ../../source/docs/selecting-a-frame.rst:44 708c4d8be7df4ec9b4751fd53d92abd3
msgid ""
"Opting for vehicles that come without RC units is suggested. This "
"recommendation stems from the fact that the RC units bundled with most "
"ready-to-run RC cars often lack the extra channel essential for autopilot "
"mode control and tuning."
msgstr "建议选择不含 RC 套件的车辆。此建议源于大多数即飞型 RC 车捆绑的 RC 套件通常缺少自动驾驶模式控制和调试所必需的额外通道。"

#: ../../source/docs/selecting-a-frame.rst:45 ecee8497f88b40c587ab6c04e3971096
msgid ""
"For increased efficiency, durability, and performance, consider a brushless "
"motor."
msgstr "为提高效率、耐用性和性能，请考虑使用无刷电机。"

#: ../../source/docs/selecting-a-frame.rst:46 df8cd3629ea748dfaddd9fe53fe2c422
msgid ""
"Consider the placement of the battery and motor on the frame. These will "
"most likely be the heaviest components on your rover and having them as low "
"as possible decreases the tendency to roll over."
msgstr "考虑电池和电机在车架上的位置。这些通常是 Rover 上最重的组件，将它们尽量放低可减少翻车倾向。"

#: ../../source/docs/selecting-a-frame.rst:47 90f5f1e604b64ec5b20f4f8131f159a3
msgid ""
"Look for a vehicle that offers ease of maintenance and component "
"replacement. You might need to replace or upgrade parts over time."
msgstr "寻找便于维护和更换组件的车辆。随着时间推移，您可能需要更换或升级零件。"

#: ../../source/docs/selecting-a-frame.rst:48 0cdbbfd619e449af9930df8af95ac77b
msgid ""
"Think about the power requirements of all components, including the "
"autopilot, to ensure your power supply can handle the load."
msgstr "考虑所有组件（包括自动驾驶仪）的电源需求，确保电源供应能够承担负载。"
